{number: 145}
{title: There is Sunshine}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There is [C] sunshine in my soul today,
More [F] glorious and [C] bright
Than glows in any earthly sky,
For [G7] Jesus is my [C] light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O there's [F] sunshine, blessed [C] sunshine,
When the [Am] peaceful, happy moments [G7] roll;
When [C] Jesus shows His smiling face,
There is [F] sunshine [G7] in the [C] soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There is [C] music in my soul today,
A [F] carol to my [C] King,
And Jesus, listening, can hear
The [G7] song I cannot [C] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
There is [C] gladness in my soul today,
And [F] hope and praise and [C] love,
For blessings which He gives me now,
For [G7] joys laid up a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}
